# scene_reader_parity — every disagreement this target has found, pinned forever.
# One decimal master seed per line; `--seed <n>` reproduces one exactly.
# See tests/fuzz/corpus/README.md for the lane contract.

# ── A revision marker of 0, which only an in-memory tree can hold as signed ──
# Found on the first run (2026-11-26). The generator built entities in memory,
# where `"$rev": 0` can be a SIGNED integer; the JSON reader refuses a signed
# revision, while the CBOR reader sees the unsigned 0 to_cbor writes. No parsed
# file holds a signed non-negative integer, so the generator now reads its entity
# back through text, as a .scene is read. Kept: both seeds put a revision marker
# on a component and exercise the migrate path in both readers.
